From: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 03:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: hash decrypted SOE packets by their inner header

The RX path sets the hash of an incoming ESP packet from its outer FOE
entry, and airoha_soe_complete_in() restores the header of that packet
onto the decrypted result, hash included. Every inner flow of an SA
therefore carries the same L4 hash: RPS steers them all to one CPU and
a flow hashing qdisc on the LAN egress puts them into one flow.

Clear the hash of the decrypted packet so that it is computed from its
own header when it is needed.

Signed-off-by: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
@@ -3233,6 +3233,11 @@ static bool airoha_soe_complete_in(struc
 	if (rx_protocol == htons(ETH_P_XDSA))
 		skb->protocol = rx_protocol;
 	skb->ip_summed = CHECKSUM_NONE;
+	/* The restored header carries the receive hash of the outer ESP
+	 * packet, which all inner flows of the SA share. Let RPS and flow
+	 * hashing qdiscs hash the decrypted packet by its own header.
+	 */
+	skb_clear_hash(skb);
 	skb_reset_mac_len(skb);
 	skb->encapsulation = 0;
 	skb->mark = xfrm_smark_get(skb->mark, x);
